  m_Name: Object_36
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Exhaust Manifold Center
  description: The Exhaust Manifold Center is a large, elongated metal component
    located at the middle-center-center of the engine, responsible for collecting
    and directing exhaust gases from the cylinders to the exhaust system. Its metal-bright
    material provides excellent heat resistance and durability, and its position
    enables efficient exhaust gas flow. Interestingly, the Exhaust Manifold Center
    is designed to work in tandem with the left and right exhaust manifolds to maintain
    engine balance and optimize exhaust gas flow.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
